{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795433113,"nonce":"f5PqrzvDWpKxew07swz9QyR9YAM=","title":"cn_demo components run out of their cards on a narrow window","message":"Reported in the window: at small widths some cn_demo components jump out of their container and overflow to the window edge.\n\n`cargo run --release -p blinc-bench --example cn_demo_widths` (new) lays the page out headlessly at each of `WIDTHS` and lists every element whose visible part passes its parent's right edge while the parent does not clip it, with the section title. At 360 px before the fix: 47 elements, 25 at 480, 9 at 640, 5 at 768.\n\nCauses, in three groups:\n- Components that cannot get narrower than their content: the menubar, navigation menu, breadcrumb and pagination (a row of triggers or buttons that never wraps; pagination squeezed its buttons), and the progress bar and chart with a set width.\n- Demo rows without `flex_wrap` (icon buttons, progress rows, number input sizes, toggles, comboboxes, hover card and tooltip triggers, tabs, tree view, charts, avatars, icons) and demo boxes with a fixed `w(..)` wider than the content (CSS card 350, form columns 300, sliders 300, tabs 500, chart wrappers 280 to 450).\n- The page's side padding is 48 px plus 16 px of section padding, leaving 232 px at 360.\n\nTwo bugs showed at every width: the small and large sliders sat side by side in one 300 px box, so the large one ran out of it; the sidebar inset used `.p(24.0)` (96 px a side), wrapping \"Icon Size Comparison\" a character per line once the window is under about 700 px.\n\nLeft after the fix, at every width and not visible as overflow: the calendar's sliding month viewport, which the check sees as wider than the calendar body; and a chart's last value tick, centred on the plot's end, a few pixels past the plot box.","files":null}]}